---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro'
import { hospital } from '../data/site'
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Refund & Cancellation Policy"
  subtitle="How appointment cancellations, no-shows, refunds and billing corrections are handled."
  updated="September 2026"
>
  <h2>1. Scope</h2>
  <p>
    This policy applies to appointment bookings, health-camp registrations, teleconsultations and any online payments made
    through the {hospital.name} website. In-person hospital services are also governed by the billing and admission
    policies provided at the time of service.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Cancelling or Rescheduling an Appointment</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Appointment booking itself is <strong>free of charge</strong> on this website.</li>
    <li>You may cancel or reschedule by calling us at <strong>{hospital.phones.appointment}</strong> or informing the front desk.</li>
    <li>Please inform us at least <strong>4 hours before</strong> your appointment slot so the slot can be offered to another patient.</li>
    <li>Repeated no-shows may lead to your future online bookings being confirmed only by phone.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>3. Consultation Fees and No-Show</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>OPD consultation fees are payable at the hospital reception unless a specific prepayment option is offered.</li>
    <li>Where a consultation fee has been prepaid online and you attend, the fee is adjusted against the services provided. Consultation fees are generally <strong>non-refundable once the consultation has taken place</strong>.</li>
    <li>If you prepaid for a consultation and do <strong>not</strong> attend (no-show) without prior cancellation, the fee may be retained or a portion adjusted against administrative costs.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>4. Online Payments and Refund Eligibility</h2>
  <p>Where online payment is enabled and you make a payment through the website:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Cancelled by the hospital:</strong> if we cancel or cannot provide the booked service, the amount paid is refunded in full.</li>
    <li><strong>Cancelled by you with notice:</strong> cancellations made at least 4 hours before the appointment are eligible for a full refund of any prepaid service charge (excluding payment-gateway charges, if any).</li>
    <li><strong>Late cancellation:</strong> cancellations within 4 hours of the slot may attract a deduction to cover administrative and blocked-slot costs.</li>
    <li><strong>No-show:</strong> prepaid amounts may be forfeited or partly adjusted, at the hospital's discretion.</li>
    <li><strong>Duplicate or failed transactions:</strong> duplicate charges and amounts debited without a confirmed booking are refunded in full.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>5. Refund Process and Timelines</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Refund requests should be raised within <strong>7 days</strong> of the transaction by contacting the hospital with your booking reference and payment details.</li>
    <li>Eligible refunds are processed within <strong>7–10 working days</strong> of approval.</li>
    <li>Refunds are made to the original payment method wherever possible. Depending on your bank or payment provider, the amount may take a further 5–7 working days to reflect in your account.</li>
    <li>A refund reference will be shared once the refund is initiated.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>6. Billing Corrections</h2>
  <p>
    If you believe a charge is incorrect, please raise it with the billing desk before discharge where possible. Verified
    billing errors are corrected and any excess amount collected is refunded in accordance with this policy.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Insurance and Cashless Claims</h2>
  <p>
    Where treatment is covered by insurance or a TPA under a cashless arrangement, the insurer/TPA's terms govern the
    settlement. Refunds of patient-borne portions, co-payments or deposits follow the hospital's billing policy and the
    insurer's decision. See our <a href="/insurance">Insurance &amp; TPA</a> page for details.
  </p>

  <h2>8. How to Raise a Refund Request</h2>
  <p>
    Contact us with your booking reference, date of service, amount paid and reason for the request:
  </p>
  <p>
    {hospital.name}<br />
    {hospital.address.line1}, {hospital.address.line2}, {hospital.address.city}, {hospital.address.state} — {hospital.address.pincode}<br />
    Email: {hospital.email}<br />
    Phone: {hospital.phones.reception}
  </p>
  <p>
    If you are not satisfied with the resolution, you may escalate through our <a href="/grievance">Grievance Redressal</a> process.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
